Here is a complete solution using a custom web component (`<x-details>`) leveraging the Shadow DOM to achieve the desired functionality.

### `x-details.js`

```javascript
/**
 * Custom web component mimicking <details> but showing an 'intro' section 
 * when collapsed, along with a visible control icon.
 */
class XDetails extends HTMLElement {
    constructor() {
        super();
        this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' });
        this._expanded = false;
    }

    connectedCallback() {
        this.render();
        this.addEventListeners();
    }

    /**
     * Renders the initial structure into the Shadow DOM.
     */
    render() {
        this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `
            <style>
                :host {
                    display: block;
                    border: 1px solid #ccc;
                    border-radius: 4px;
                    margin-bottom: 10px;
                }
                .container {
                    display: flex;
                    flex-direction: column;
                }
                .header-row {
                    display: flex;
                    align-items: center;
                    padding: 10px 15px;
                    cursor: pointer;
                    border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
                    background-color: #f9f9f9;
                    font-size: 1.1em;
                    font-weight: bold;
                }
                .control-icon {
                    width: 20px;
                    height: 20px;
                    display: flex;
                    align-items: center;
                    justify-content: center;
                    margin-right: 10px;
                    font-size: 1.2em;
                    border: 1px solid #333;
                    border-radius: 3px;
                    background-color: #fff;
                }
                .content-wrapper {
                    padding: 0 15px;
                }
                .intro-content {
                    padding: 15px 0;
                    border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
                    margin-bottom: 10px;
                }
                .details-content {
                    padding: 15px 0;
                    display: none; /* Hidden by default */
                }
                .expand-button {
                    padding: 10px 15px;
                    background-color: #007bff;
                    color: white;
                    border: none;
                    border-radius: 4px;
                    cursor: pointer;
                    font-size: 1em;
                    transition: background-color 0.2s;
                }
                .expand-button:hover {
                    background-color: #0056b3;
                }
                .hidden {
                    display: none;
                }
            </style>

            <div class="container">
                <div class="header-row">
                    <span class="control-icon" data-state-icon>+</span>
                    <slot name="header"></slot>
                </div>

                <div class="content-wrapper">
                    <!-- Intro Part (Always Visible) -->
                    <div class="intro-content" id="intro-slot">
                        <slot name="intro"></slot>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Expand More Button (Only visible when collapsed) -->
                    <button class="expand-button" id="expand-button">Expand More</button>

                    <!-- Details Part (Visible when expanded) -->
                    <div class="details-content" id="details-slot">
                        <slot name="details"></slot>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        `;
    }

    /**
     * Attaches event listeners to handle clicks.
     */
    addEventListeners() {
        // 1. Listener for the header row to toggle state
        this.shadowRoot.querySelector('.header-row').addEventListener('click', () => this.toggle());

        // 2. Listener for the explicit 'Expand More' button
        this.shadowRoot.getElementById('expand-button').addEventListener('click', () => this.toggle());
    }

    /**
     * Toggles the expanded/collapsed state of the component.
     */
    toggle() {
        this._expanded = !this._expanded;
        this.updateView();
    }

    /**
     * Updates the CSS classes and content visibility based on the current state.
     */
    updateView() {
        const icon = this.shadowRoot.querySelector('[data-state-icon]');
        const detailsSlot = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('details-slot');
        const expandButton = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('expand-button');

        if (this._expanded) {
            // Expanded State
            icon.textContent = '−'; // Minus sign
            detailsSlot.style.display = 'block';
            expandButton.classList.add('hidden'); // Hide the expand button
        } else {
            // Collapsed State
            icon.textContent = '+'; // Plus sign
            detailsSlot.style.display = 'none'; // Hide the details content
            expandButton.classList.remove('hidden'); // Show the expand button
        }
    }
}

// Define the custom element
customElements.define('x-details', XDetails);
```

### HTML Usage Example

To use this component, save the JavaScript above as `x-details.js` and include it before your HTML.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>XDetails Component Demo</title>
    <!-- Link the component script -->
    <script src="x-details.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Custom X-Details Component Example</h1>

    <!-- Example 1: Standard Usage -->
    <x-details>
        <span slot="header">Project Overview (Click to Toggle)</span>

        <div slot="intro">
            This is the summary section. It is always visible, even when the full details are collapsed. This gives the user immediate context before deciding to expand.
        </div>

        <div slot="details">
            <h2>Detailed Technical Specifications</h2>
            <p>This section contains all the in-depth information, such as API endpoints, dependency lists, and architectural diagrams. It is hidden by default.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Component State: Ready</li>
                <li>Last Updated: Today</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </x-details>

    <!-- Example 2: Minimal Usage -->
    <x-details>
        <span slot="header">Quick Notes</span>
        <div slot="intro">A very short preamble.</div>
        <div slot="details">The long, detailed note here.</div>
    </x-details>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation of the Implementation

1.  **Shadow DOM Structure:**
    *   The component initializes by attaching a Shadow Root (`this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' });`).
    *   The HTML structure is injected into the shadow root, containing slots (`<slot name="...">`) for `header`, `intro`, and `details`.
    *   Crucially, the CSS is scoped entirely within the Shadow DOM, ensuring it doesn't leak out or get affected by external styles.

2.  **Layout and Styling (CSS):**
    *   We use `display: flex` on the `.header-row` to neatly align the `+`/`-` icon next to the header content.
    *   The `.header-row` has the required border and font styling.
    *   The `.intro-content` is styled to be the visible part below the header.
    *   The `.details-content` is set to `display: none` initially.
    *   The `.expand-button` is styled for the call-to-action when collapsed.

3.  **Functionality (`toggle()` and `updateView()`):**
    *   **State Management:** The private property `this._expanded` tracks whether the component is currently open or closed.
    *   **Event Handling:** Clicks on *both* the header row and the explicit "Expand More" button call `this.toggle()`.
    *   **Toggling:** `toggle()` simply flips `this._expanded` and then calls `updateView()`.
    *   **View Update:** `updateView()` handles the UI logic:
        *   It updates the `textContent` of the icon (`+` or `−`).
        *   It dynamically sets the `display` style of the `.details-content` slot.
        *   It shows or hides the "Expand More" button based on the state.

4.  **Slot Utilization:**
    *   **`slot="header"`:** Populates the clickable header element.
    *   **`slot="intro"`:** Populates the content visible immediately below the header when collapsed.
    *   **`slot="details"`:** Populates the content that is only revealed when the component is expanded.

